{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem remembered Sarah as He had said.</b> In conception. <b>And HaShem did for Sarah as He had spoken</b> — in birth. Thus it immediately says, ״ותהר ותלד״ — and she conceived and gave birth. And this pericah is adjoined to the pericah of ״כי עצור עצר ה״״ — to make known that the Holy One, blessed be He, is the One who shuts and He is the One who remembers, and there is none besides Him." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״וה׳ פקד את שרה״ — as it is written (Ezekiel 17:24): ״And all the trees of the field shall know that I am HaShem; I have brought down the high tree, I have exalted the low tree, I have dried up the moist tree, and I have made the dry tree flourish; I am HaShem, I have spoken and I have done it.״ ״I have brought down the high tree״ — this is Sennacherib, as it is said, ״Behold, the Assyrian was a cedar in Lebanon, fair of stature.״ ״I have exalted the low tree״ — these are Israel, who humble themselves, as it is said (Malachi 2:9): ״And I also have made you contemptible and lowly.״ ״I have dried up the moist tree״ — Avimelekh, as it is said: ״כי עצור עצר ה׳״. ״And I have made the dry tree flourish״ — this is Sarah. ״I am HaShem, I have spoken and I have done it.״ ״וה׳ פקד את שרה״ — what is פקד? Rabbi Yitzchak said: it is written (Numbers 5:28), ״ואם לא נטמאה האשה וטהורה היא״ — and she entered the house of Pharaoh and emerged pure; she entered the house of Avimelekh and emerged pure — it is not fitting that she be remembered. Hence you say, ״וה׳ פקד את שרה.״ Thus far in Bereshit Rabbah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "Source writes 'יחזקאל ה׳' (Ezekiel 5); the quoted verses correspond to Ezekiel 17:24 and Isaiah 10:33 / 37:24; rendered citation as printed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:57.723276403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}